WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.235
-From the first film, we know

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.336
that you are sort of the cooler
of the two dads.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You and Will --

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.339 size:84% position:42%
I think it comes across
in the clip, as well.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.607
What about -- You have children.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.942
You had a premiere for the film.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:11.044
Do they think it´s cool
that their dad is Mark Wahlberg?

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.212
Did they come to the premiere?

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They did not come
to the premiere.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-They basically refused

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.950 size:88% position:44%
to come to the premiere.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why -- Why did they refuse?
-They were like, "Dad,

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
we´ll see it
whenever we see it."

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m like, "Come on, everybody
is going to be there.

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.490
Will´s going to be there.
John Cena is going to be there."

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.891 size:78% position:39%
They had no interest.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.726
And, of course, Will shows up
with his wife and the kids

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they´re all in suits and
dressed up and --

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
they just didn´t want to go.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.267
The boys were watching football.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
My daughter is on the phone,
doing her thing.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do they just -- Do you think
it´s that they aged out

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.173 size:88% position:44%
of their dad being cool?

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think your heyday
of being a cool dad is over?

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s been over.
-Okay.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.345
-You know, so now I´m like,

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.080 size:75% position:38%
I don´t make a point
to embarrass them,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.416
but I´m not going to try to hide
my affection for them either.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.284
So, they´re like, "Dad, drop us
off in the alley at the school."

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m like "No.
I´m going to walk you in.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m getting a kiss
in front of all your friends.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:55.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that´s it."

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.024
But, if they need something,

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.627
if they want to meet Drake,
or they want somebody that,

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, they know Dad knows
or can hookup...

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.863
-Yeah.
-...then they´ll say, "Oh, yeah

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dad, we think you´re cool
for five minutes."

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.868
So they´re not smart enough,
if they want to meet Drake,

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
to, like, be nice for a week
leading up to the ask?

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
They just --
-For a week? No.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´ll be nice
for five minutes.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.775
If they don´t get
what they want, when they want,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.377 size:84% position:42%
they´re just right back
to not talking to me

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:20.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
or just, you know, being,
you know, kids.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:23.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, they´re kids,
so I understand.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m not that --
My son is a year and a half,

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.753 size:75% position:38%
and he´s just super.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.388
I think he thinks I´m the
coolest dude he´s ever met

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause he´s only met
like six dudes.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.592
-Enjoy it while it lasts.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.793 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah, I´m going to.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.928 size:81% position:41%
-And more importantly,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
be grateful
that it´s not a girl.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, now, mind you,
the best relationship

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.468
that I have with my daughter --

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:42.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
Daddy/daughter relationship
is great,

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:45.672
but when they become teenagers,
something happens.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have no idea
what to do about it,

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
how to handle it.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.043
The hormones, the emotions.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:52.879
It´s absolute torture, so --

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, watch out.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.715 size:78% position:39%
-That´s really sweet.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it´s sweet
until it happens to you.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
And like I said, we´re cool.
But you know what?

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
The whole thing with the boys
and all of this stuff,

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.891
I´m just not ready for it.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I gotcha.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:10.363
So, I want to ask about this
because Will was here yesterday

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I didn´t have a chance
to ask him about it.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.666 size:78% position:39%
But your assistant --

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did your assistant get a part
in the film in the end?

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He got a part in the end,
but he got cut.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, he got cut.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and he only auditioned
for like one line.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
One word, really.
-Okay.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
He´s yelling one word
in the audience

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.547
of the -- the improv club.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we made him audition
to Tim Hutton´s

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.818 size:78% position:39%
most emotional scenes
in "Ordinary People."

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] So wait --
-And he spent weeks and weeks

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:37.056
and weeks studying these scenes,
learning the lines.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he emoted
in front of me and Will

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.994
and Chris Henchy for like --

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you made him audition
in front --

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:43.963
He didn´t have to audition.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
He auditioned for you
and Will and Chris Henchy.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We are the producers
of the film.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:50.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
We basically said, "Yes.
You have to do this."

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know what?
He did a good job.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.473
But then they -- he didn´t --

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
he did a good job
in the audition,

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
but maybe didn´t do a good job
in the actual scene.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.111 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, so you had to --
-So the scene got cut.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:00.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
What can I do?
But I told Tim Hutton.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.949 size:84% position:42%
Tim Hutton and I worked
on a movie after that,

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I told him, and Tim really
wanted to see the footage.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really?
Did you show --

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.588
-I didn´t get it in time.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:09.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don´t think
he would have --

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think at first he thought
we were paying homage,

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.193
but then I think I realized

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he might not
have liked it after he saw it.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wasn´t quite
up to Tim´s standards.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, exactly.
-Won an Oscar for that part.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He did win an Oscar
for that part.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
I forgot that.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.104
Now, I also heard that --
so Will -- John Lithgow

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
plays Will´s father.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.007
-And they have a fight scene.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.275 size:81% position:41%
And you encourage them

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just to go for it
when you were shooting it,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:34.080
but to like actually physically
go for it in rehearsal.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.915 size:81% position:41%
-John is a method guy.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.050
Will is -- You know how Will --
-Yeah.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.484
-He´s a such sweet guy, right?

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he doesn´t want
to say anything to John.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, like, you know, when they
had to do the first

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.356
big, long, awkward kiss, right,

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m like, "Oh,
that was really good.

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:45.892
You guys got to do that again."

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I keep telling John,
"Do it more often."

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then John is doing it
at rehearsals,

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:51.264
he´s doing it when
they´re just blocking the scene.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Will
would never say anything,

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I could tell
he was getting annoyed.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.836
So I would start, you know --
It was giving me great pleasure.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And then when they started

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.839 size:81% position:41%
doing the fight scene,

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, John was just, like,
putting him in a headlock.

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:02.909
And you could tell Will --

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause, like, we did 15 takes
of the first scene

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I had to give him
a heart pump

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.348 size:81% position:41%
and try to revive him.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:09.515
And he didn´t say anything

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
until, like, I almost caved
his chest in.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was like, "Maybe now
that you got the hard one in,

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.921
you do one of those soft ones.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:16.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
You probably have
a soft one in you."

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.790 size:75% position:38%
So I´m like, "Okay."

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, and then John
was just torturing him.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.226 size:75% position:38%
It was a lot of fun.

